  - title: 
    basic: Here you can see insulin monomers group into dimers, and then form a hexamer,
      the basic subunit of the insulin crystal.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: The hexamer formation process is dependent on the zinc concentration in
      the insulin vesicle.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: 
    basic: The kinetics of insulin oligerization has great discrepancies in studies,
      however it is believed that hexamer formation is about 100x slower than dimerization.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
